{title: Faces Like Lions}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 12:1–14; 12:8; 12:12; 12:15; 12:16–22}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×13
| [Bbmaj7] | [Bbmaj7] | [C] | [C] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
David at Ziklag in the [Bb]wild
Saul the king kept him confined
Men with bows and slings came near
[C]From Benjamin they joined the [Dm]field
Ahiezer and Joash lead
Shemaah's sons from Gibeon
[Bb]Armed with shield and spear in [C]hand
Facing the battle [Dm]ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Their faces like [C]the faces of li[Bb]ons
Swift as ga[C]zelles on the moun[Dm]tains
Mighty war[C]riors in the [Bb]fight
With [C]shields and spears held [Dm]tight
The [Bb]Gadite [C]men so [Dm]brave
[Bb]Crossed the Jordan [C]in the [Dm]wave
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Ezer the chief Obadiah two
Eliab third in the crew
[Bb]Mishmannah four Jeremiah [C]five
Attai six with Eliel's [Dm]drive
Johanan eight and Elzabad ninth
Jeremiah tenth in the depth
[Bb]Machbannai the eleventh [C]man
Strongest of the Gadite [Bb]clan
The least [C]for a hundred [Bb]men
The greatest [C]for a [Dm]thousand then
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Their faces [C]like the faces of li[Bb]ons
Swift as ga[C]zelles on the moun[Dm]tains
Mighty war[C]riors in the [Bb]fight
With [C]shields and spears held [Dm]tight
The [Bb]Gadite [C]men so [Dm]brave
[Bb]Crossed the Jordan in [C]the [Dm]wave
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]First month the [C]river overflo[Dm]wed
[Bb]Driving [C]out the valley [Dm]road
They [Bb]crossed the Jordan [C]stream
To help [Dm]David with his dream
[Bb]Peace to [C]you son of Jesse
We are with you in dis[Dm]tress
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Their faces like [C]the faces of li[Dm]ons
Swift as ga[C]zelles on the moun[Dm]tains
Mighty war[C]riors in the [Bb]fight
With [C]shields and spears held [Dm]tight
The [Bb]Gadite [C]men so [Dm]brave
[Bb]Crossed the Jordan [C]in the [Dm]wave
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [C] | [Dm] | [Dm] | ×4

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bbmaj7]Elzabad ninth among [C]the brave
[Dm]A name in David's army grave
{end_of_verse}
